      "tr": "`smaller`, `equal`, `larger` listelerini kavramayla kur.",
      "en": "Build the `smaller`, `equal`, `larger` lists with comprehensions."
    },
    {
      "tr": "`k < len(smaller)` → solda; `k < len(smaller) + len(equal)` → `return pivot`; yoksa `k`'dan iki boyu çıkar ve sağa geç.",
      "en": "`k < len(smaller)` → left; `k < len(smaller) + len(equal)` → `return pivot`; otherwise subtract both lengths from `k` and move right."
    },
    {
      "tr": "Çözümün tamamı:\n\n```python\nimport random\n\n\ndef kth_smallest(values, k):\n    items = list(values)\n    while True:\n        pivot = random.choice(items)\n        smaller = [x for x in items if x < pivot]\n        equal = [x for x in items if x == pivot]\n        if k < len(smaller):\n            items = smaller\n        elif k < len(smaller) + len(equal):\n            return pivot\n        else:\n            k -= len(smaller) + len(equal)\n            items = [x for x in items if x > pivot]\n\nvalues = [7, 2, 9, 4, 4, 1, 8]\nprint(kth_smallest(values, 0), kth_smallest(values, 3), kth_smallest(values, 6))\nrng = random.Random(5)\nbig = [rng.randint(0, 10**6) for _ in range(200_001)]\nprint(kth_smallest(big, 100_000))\n```",
      "en": "The full solution:\n\n```python\nimport random\n\n\ndef kth_smallest(values, k):\n    items = list(values)\n    while True:\n        pivot = random.choice(items)\n        smaller = [x for x in items if x < pivot]\n        equal = [x for x in items if x == pivot]\n        if k < len(smaller):\n            items = smaller\n        elif k < len(smaller) + len(equal):\n            return pivot\n        else:\n            k -= len(smaller) + len(equal)\n            items = [x for x in items if x > pivot]\n\nvalues = [7, 2, 9, 4, 4, 1, 8]\nprint(kth_smallest(values, 0), kth_smallest(values, 3), kth_smallest(values, 6))\nrng = random.Random(5)\nbig = [rng.randint(0, 10**6) for _ in range(200_001)]\nprint(kth_smallest(big, 100_000))\n```"
    }
